Need consider edge detection across calls: prev flags updated at end. If a request is TRUE on first call, rise true. Next call if TRUE still, prev true, rise false. Good.

Need consider if request is TRUE on first call and we process, then prev updated to TRUE. If request goes FALSE next call, rise false, idle clears outputs. Good.

Need consider if request goes TRUE then FALSE then TRUE, edges detected. Good.

Need maybe if multiple rising, we update prev to all true, so next scan no rise even if still true. Good.

Need maybe if riseCount=0 and some inputs true but prev true, idle clears. Good.

Need maybe if riseCount=0 but inputs false, idle clears. Good.

Need maybe if a request is rising and another is already true from previous scan? Assumption: at most one rising edge per call; simultaneous rising edges across all four outside valid domain. But what if addRecipe rises while deleteRecipe is held true? riseAdd true, riseDelete false (prev true). riseCount=1. We would process add. Is that allowed? The assumption says "At most one request rising edge may occur per call; simultaneous rising edges across addRecipe, deleteRecipe, modifyRecipe, and queryRecipe are outside the valid domain." It doesn't forbid one rising while another held. But typically only one request signal at a time. If another held true, we might process the rising one. That's okay per rising edge semantics. The idle condition is no rising request, regardless levels. So if delete held true and add rises, we process add. The delete held true doesn't matter. Good.

Need maybe if riseCount=0 but some request true (held), idle clears outputs. That matches "idle: no rising request". Good.

Need ensure on idle, error/status clear even if previous error. Yes.

Need maybe if a request rises and fails, error true status code. Next scan if request still true, no rising, idle clears error/status. That matches one-invocation error? The spec says "error/status clear on idle." If request remains true, it's not idle (no rising request? Wait idle is defined as no rising request. If request remains true, there is no rising request, so idle condition is true! So error/status clear on next scan. That's correct: error only lasts one scan? The requirements: "When a query recipe request signal (queryRecipe) is triggered" likely on rising edge. If signal held, only triggered once. Error output maybe should stay while signal held? But LTL says idle = no rising request, and clear = NOT error AND status=0... So on next scan with held signal, no rising, idle true, so error must clear. So our implementation clears on every scan at start and only sets on rising. If held true, next scan rise false, outputs clear. Good. That matches.

